 ## Overview
-NeILF (Neural Inverse Lighting Field) is a rendering pipeline that decomposes 3D Gaussian Splatting features into physically based diffuse, specular, and ambient components using a Blinn-Phong model, enabling inverse rendering via specialized loss functions on depth, normals, and color sparsity [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard Gaussian Splatting by explicitly modeling lighting interactions through learnable material parameters (diffuse factor, shininess, ambient factor, specular factor) rather than relying solely on view-dependent color encoding [S1, unofficial].
+NeILF (Neural Inverse Lighting Field) is a rendering pipeline that decomposes Gaussian Splatting features into diffuse, specular, and ambient components using a Blinn-Phong model, enabling inverse rendering via loss functions on depth, normals, and color sparsity [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard Gaussian Splatting by explicitly modeling lighting interactions through learnable material factors (diffuse, specular, ambient) and supporting multi-Gaussian group rendering with palette-based color offsets, allowing for physically plausible relighting and material optimization [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
+
+### Inputs and Outputs
 **Inputs:**
-- Camera parameters: pose (view matrix $W$), intrinsics ($f_x, f_y, c_x, c_y$), resolution ($H, W$) [S1, unofficial].
-- 3D Gaussian primitives: position, covariance $\Sigma$, opacity $\alpha$, and feature vectors including `diffuse_factor`, `shininess`, `ambient_factor`, `specular_factor`, and `offset_color` [S1, unofficial].
-- Light configuration: `light_transform` (optional transformation for light direction) [S1, unofficial].
-- Ground truth: `gt_image`, `gt_depth`, `image_mask`, `depth_mask` [S1, unofficial].
-- Optimization weights: `lambda_render`, `lambda_phong`, `lambda_depth`, `lambda_opacity`, `lambda_normal_render_depth`, `lambda_normal_mvs_depth`, `lambda_offset_color_sparsity`, `lambda_diffuse_factor_smooth`, `lambda_ambient_factor_smooth`, `lambda_normal_smooth`, `lambda_dssim` [S1, unofficial].
-- `sample_num`: Number of incident rays sampled for normal-based lighting, default 24 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `primitives`: A set of 3D Gaussians, each containing position, covariance, opacity, and feature vectors (diffuse_factor, offset_color, shininess, ambient_factor, specular_factor) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `camera`: Camera pose (view matrix), intrinsics (focal length, principal point), and resolution [S1, unofficial].
+*   `light_transform`: Optional transformation for light direction and intensity factors (diffuse_factor, shininess, ambient_factor, specular_factor) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `opt`: Optimization configuration including loss weights (`lambda_render`, `lambda_phong`, `lambda_depth`, `lambda_opacity`, `lambda_normal_render_depth`, `lambda_normal_mvs_depth`, `lambda_offset_color_sparsity`, `lambda_diffuse_factor_smooth`, `lambda_ambient_factor_smooth`, `lambda_normal_smooth`, `lambda_dssim`) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `is_training`: Boolean flag indicating if the pipeline is in training mode (affects loss calculation) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `num_GSs_TFs`: List of counts of Gaussians per transformation group (for multi-Gaussian rendering) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `palette_colors`: List of base colors for each transformation group [S1, unofficial].
+*   `opacity_factors`: List of opacity scaling factors for each transformation group [S1, unofficial].
