+### Parameters
+*   `sample_num`: Number of incident rays sampled for normal-based lighting, default 24 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_render`: Optimization weight for render loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_phong`: Optimization weight for Phong loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_depth`: Optimization weight for depth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_opacity`: Optimization weight for opacity loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_normal_render_depth`: Optimization weight for normal render depth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_normal_mvs_depth`: Optimization weight for normal MVS depth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_offset_color_sparsity`: Optimization weight for offset color sparsity loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_diffuse_factor_smooth`: Optimization weight for diffuse factor smooth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_ambient_factor_smooth`: Optimization weight for ambient factor smooth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_normal_smooth`: Optimization weight for normal smooth loss [S1, unofficial].
+*   `lambda_dssim`: Weight for SSIM component in L1+SSIM loss [S1, unofficial].
+
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   Gaussians with radius 0 or frustum culled are excluded from value updates in splitting criteria via `visibility_filter` (radii > 0) [S1, unofficial].
+*   MVS normal map may be all zeros; in this case, pseudo normal is computed from `gt_depth` using `kornia.depth_to_normals` and transformed to world space [S1, unofficial].
+*   Precision issues may arise when computing `cos_l != 0` for specular intensity; use a small epsilon if necessary [G].
+*   Clamping of colors and opacities is essential to prevent NaN values during optimization [S1, unofficial].
